 @code{endemph} (@pxopref{endemph}) is the counterpart of
 @code{endmode} for indication of emphasis.
+
+@opcode{endcapsphrase, before|after|afterletters dots}
+Define the terminator for a capitals passage introduced by
+@code{begcapsphrase}. @code{before} places it before the final word;
+@code{after} includes trailing punctuation in that word.
+The forward-translation option @code{afterletters} ends the passage after
+its last cased letter. Punctuation, digits, signs, and caseless letters
+break such a passage. This lets tables for mixed-script text choose
+their own boundary behavior without changing the default used by UEB.
+
+@opcode{capsphrasevar, variable}
+Expose the sentence-wide capitals-passage analysis to forward context
+rules through a multipass variable numbered 1 to 49. At each input
+position the engine sets the variable to 1 inside a capitals passage,
+including its ending boundary, or 0 outside. The value is recomputed
+by input position, including after zero-width context actions and
+translation rewinds. Tables should reserve this variable for tests,
+not assign to it. No capitals-passage analysis is performed by the
+context rules themselves.
 
 @opcode{letsign, dots}
